WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.600
Now most famous as Netflix's surprise hit
of the 2019 holiday season, The Witcher started

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.630
life as a series of fantasy books and short
stories written by Polish author Andrzej Sapkowski.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:15.480
The franchise's fortunes really took off in
2007, when game developers CD Projekt Red

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.940
produced the first of three smash hit video
games based on The Witcher.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.000
It was in the games that Triss Merigold went
from a magic-wielding secondary character

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.390
lusting after the titular monster-slayer Geralt
to a magic-wielding major character and Geralt's

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.180
actual, though occasional, love interest.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:35.010
In November 2018, British actress Anna Shaffer
was announced for the role in the Netflix

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:35.620
adaptation.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.940
Given the character's contradicting history
between the page and the games, fans wondered

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.800
whether the Witcher writers would lean into
Triss' romance with Geralt on the series,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.750
or return to the original text and sideline
her in favor of other characters.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.730
On the first season of The Witcher at least,
it looked as though they were leaning more

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:55.310
towards the books, with Shaffer's Triss maintaining
a platonic-slash-professional relationship

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:58.900
with Geralt and ultimately working more closely
with the sorceress Yennefer.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.420
"I enlisted a Witcher.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.220
Geralt of Rivia.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.900
I often wonder where fate took him."

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.540
"Somewhere unpleasant, I'm sure."

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.990
No matter what the Witcher team chose to do
with Triss Merigold for the show, one thing

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.520
is undeniable: the actress who plays her looks
incredibly familiar.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.720
Here's where you may have seen Anna Shaffer
before.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.220
Anna Shaffer's first-ever screen role was
in 2009's Harry Potter and the Half-Blood

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.700
Prince, in which she played a witch who couldn't
land her romantic interest.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:27.540
Sound familiar?

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.980
In the David Yates-directed film, Shaffer
portrayed Gryffindor student Romilda Vane,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.470
the leader of a clique of girls who become
obsessed with Harry, or, rather, with his

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.240
celebrity status, and trail him around Hogwarts
trying to get his attention.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.080
In case you've forgotten the small details
from Harry Potter, Romilda Vane was a small

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.040
but memorable character in the fifth film.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:49.180
Remember when Harry's best pal Ron Weasley
accidentally ate a Chocolate Cauldron laced

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.360
with love potion and became instantly infatuated
with a girl?

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.420
That girl was Romilda, who actually made the
love potion specifically for Harry.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:01.120
Shaffer also appeared in the last two movies
of the franchise, 2010's Harry Potter and

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.330
the Deathly Hallows Part 1 and 2011's Part
2 continuation, but her character had a more

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.440
serious purpose throughout those installments.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.840
Romilda joins Dumbledore's Army to fight against
the evil forces taking over the wizarding

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:17.380
world, but unlike many other minor characters,
she survives the Battle of Hogwarts that left

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.200
dozens dead.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.760
Shaffer has a connection to another beloved
British-born franchise, one arguably even

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.880
more popular than Harry Potter and one that's
certainly been around for a lot longer.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:31.460
The actress appeared briefly on Class, a Doctor
Who spin-off series written and created by

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.480
Patrick Ness.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:36.760
The show centered around a group of teenagers
studying at Coal Hill Academy, a fictional

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.760
school that has popped up on numerous occasions
throughout Doctor Who, and the staff who worked

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.260
there.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.900
On the series, which lasted only one season,
Shaffer played Rachel Chapman, the girlfriend

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.560
of main character Ram, who comes to a nasty
end, only for him to move on to another love

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.520
interest a couple of episodes later.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.080
So much for the power of love.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:59.060
Outside of worlds populated by witches, aliens,
and would-be girlfriends, Shaffer has mostly

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.560
been left with minor roles.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.960
She had a blink-and-you'll-miss-it part in
the widely praised BBC drama Fearless in 2017,

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.370
and before The Witcher, she popped up in the
background of the forgettable British action

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.780
movie I Am Vengeance.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:14.860
However, Shaffer managed to make a mark in
a super-melodramatic TV series.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:18.720
She played yet another troublemaker with a
deeply hidden heart of gold when she took

00:03:18.739 --> 00:03:23.010
on the role of rebellious bully Ruby Button
on the British daily soap opera Hollyoaks

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:29.340
from 2011 to 2014, returning for four guest
appearances in 2017 and 2018.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.560
In typical soap fashion, Shaffer's Ruby went
through a lot during her brief stint on Hollyoaks:

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:39.010
a hit-and-run in which she was the passenger,
a foiled elopement that ended in her fiancé's

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:43.319
death, social exile on account of all the
bullying she'd masterminded, a cocaine-induced

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.440
heart attack, and a new life in Spain.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.780
It almost makes dealing with the respective
armies of Voldemort, the Shadow Kin, and the

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.660
Nilfgaard seem like a cakewalk.

